1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:07,590
Tonight, the peepal tree hosts a wedding… the kind this village hasn't seen in two hundred years.

2
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:11,081
Dadi, my heart is pounding!

3
00:00:11,331 --> 00:00:14,021
Since when does a ghost's heart beat?

4
00:00:14,271 --> 00:00:16,769
Since today. It's my wedding day.

5
00:00:17,019 --> 00:00:20,373
Fine, let's check the list. Is everything ready?

6
00:00:26,823 --> 00:00:31,915
Just one problem, Dadi. No human guests are coming.

7
00:00:32,165 --> 00:00:33,990
Why? Did you invite them?

8
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:39,571
I did. At midnight, from the peepal tree, at the top of my voice.

9
00:00:39,821 --> 00:00:43,714
Then the whole village has locked its doors and gone to sleep.

10
00:00:43,964 --> 00:00:48,253
See? I CAN scare people! Just not in front of them.

11
00:00:48,503 --> 00:00:51,689
Never mind. I'm your human guest, aren't I?

12
00:00:52,039 --> 00:00:54,552
…Dadi, you'll really come?

13
00:00:54,802 --> 00:00:58,238
Come where? The wedding is right here in my courtyard.

14
00:00:59,988 --> 00:01:09,793
Midnight. The baraat is ready. The guests: two owls, four bats… and a frog who got lost on the way.

15
00:01:10,043 --> 00:01:16,038
Dadi, I'll make my entry scary! Smoke, noises, chains!

16
00:01:16,288 --> 00:01:18,941
At a wedding you don't scare people. You dance.

17
00:01:19,191 --> 00:01:21,406
But I can't dance!

18
00:01:21,656 --> 00:01:26,199
You can't scare either. You've still been at it for two hundred years.

19
00:01:29,649 --> 00:01:32,212
Enough, enough. Even the frog is scared.

20
00:01:32,462 --> 00:01:35,037
See! I scared someone!

21
00:01:35,287 --> 00:01:38,077
A frog isn't a human, Chaman.

22
00:01:40,627 --> 00:01:44,549
Who has come to marry my daughter?

23
00:01:44,799 --> 00:01:47,219
M-mother-in-law! Namaste! I'm Chaman!

24
00:01:47,469 --> 00:01:53,670
I don't come out of the well. I'll ask from right here. How many people have you scared?

25
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:58,612
…Zero. But today I scared a frog!

26
00:01:58,862 --> 00:02:04,458
Zero?! In three hundred years my daughter has emptied three villages!

27
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:06,900
And how many dishes has she washed?

28
00:02:08,350 --> 00:02:10,222
…Not a single one.

29
00:02:10,472 --> 00:02:15,540
Then it's an equal match. The boy doesn't scare, the girl doesn't wash dishes.

30
00:02:15,790 --> 00:02:19,909
…Who is this Dadi? She scares me.

31
00:02:20,159 --> 00:02:23,219
Everyone feels that, mother-in-law. Everyone.

32
00:02:26,569 --> 00:02:30,123
And then… out of the well came the bride. Chandni.

33
00:02:30,373 --> 00:02:34,321
Chandni ji… you look… absolutely terrifying.

34
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:37,888
Thank you. You look… alright too.

35
00:02:38,138 --> 00:02:39,841
Come on, the garlands.

36
00:02:42,291 --> 00:02:44,817
That's it. You two are now husband and wife.

37
00:02:46,767 --> 00:02:48,740
Did the power go?

38
00:02:48,990 --> 00:02:51,519
Shhh… someone's behind the courtyard.

39
00:02:53,369 --> 00:02:57,777
Heh heh… everyone's busy at the wedding. I'll grab the old lady's trunk.

40
00:02:58,027 --> 00:03:00,463
A thief! Chaman ji, do something!

41
00:03:00,713 --> 00:03:03,370
M-me? Nobody is ever scared of me!

42
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:07,845
Chaman. It's your wedding day. If not today, then never.

43
00:03:09,795 --> 00:03:15,596
Ha ha ha! I am Chaman Bhoot! I've lived in this peepal tree for two hundred years!

44
00:03:15,846 --> 00:03:17,859
G-g-ghost! Help! Mummy!

45
00:03:20,709 --> 00:03:23,383
He… he got scared? He really got scared?!

46
00:03:23,633 --> 00:03:26,168
He did. He even left his slippers behind.

47
00:03:28,418 --> 00:03:33,016
My husband scared a human! Oh, how brave he is!

48
00:03:33,266 --> 00:03:35,990
It took two hundred years… but I did it!

49
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:44,262
Dawn was breaking. And a letter arrived from the Ghost Union.

50
00:03:51,212 --> 00:03:53,784
Dadi! I'm a full ghost now!

51
00:03:54,034 --> 00:03:56,867
Congratulations. And now there are two ghosts in this house…

52
00:03:57,117 --> 00:03:58,628
Yes, Dadi?

53
00:03:58,878 --> 00:04:01,656
So the rent is for two now.

54
00:04:01,906 --> 00:04:03,107
Dadi!

55
00:04:03,357 --> 00:04:06,552
Ha ha ha! I like this house.

56
00:04:08,902 --> 00:04:17,758
And from that day on, two ghosts live in the peepal tree… and in the courtyard, a Dadi who's afraid of no one.

